{
  "scope": "Two periodic tangents, one free normal, prepared by bringing two separately converted law-1 samples into contact. Each branch uses identical coordinates at first contact, site temperature, projected area, free faces, Brownian increments and durations. The two samples have distinct seeds. All laws receive one undriven contact-formation transit before the 1-transit deformation hold. Directional shear readings are restored from the earlier measurement. Projected-area response and the two isotropic shear responses are new.",
  "definitions": {
    "shear": "Derivative of (sigma_xx-sigma_yy) with respect to gamma for e^(+gamma),e^(-gamma).",
    "area": "For log-area change h, x and y scale by exp(h/2). P=(N*kBT-dU/dh)/A uses the instantaneous projected area. K=-dP/dh. The free-normal height remains dynamical.",
    "amplitudes": [
      0.0001,
      5e-05
    ],
    "late": "Arithmetic mean over frames 37 to 48 inclusive."
  },
